Verify that optional G76 X endpoints produce tapered XZ drive lines while
preserving axial P pitch.  The canonical trace covers absolute and incremental
endpoints, radius and diameter mode, internal and external threads, both drive
line slopes, entry/exit taper in both Z directions, compound infeed, and spring
passes. Compound-infeed coverage verifies fixed-direction G76 and
alternating-flank G76.1 on tapered and cylindrical drive lines, plus centered Q0
paths, and that no G76.1 pass, mirrored ones included, feeds past either end
of the programmed Z range (alternating-z-range.ngc). Every cycle runs inside the spindle override hold (LOCK_SPEED_OVERRIDE
before the first pass, ENABLE_SPEED_OVERRIDE after the last). Negative tests
verify, by message, that G76 rejects a Y endpoint, a tapered drive line with no
Z length, a D word, and G76 together with G76.1 in one block.

The pitch check against the axis velocity limits needs a machine and is tested
in ../../g76-tapered-pitch.
